14997      data Crops;
14998      length Crop $ 10;
14999      infile datalines truncover;
15000      input Crop $ @@;
15001      do i=1 to 3;
15002      input x1-x4 @@;
15003      if (x1 ^= .) then output;
15004      end;
15005      input;
15006      datalines;

NOTE: The data set WORK.CROPS has 36 observations and 6 variables.

15020      ;
15021      ods graphics on;
15022      proc logistic data=Crops;
15023      model Crop=x1-x4 / link=glogit;
15024      score out=Score1;
15025      effectplot slicefit(x=x3);
15026      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is fitting the generalized logit model. The logits modeled contrast each response level against the reference level (Crop='Sugarbeets'). 
      Use the response variable option REF= if you want to change the reference level.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: There were 36 observations read from the data set WORK.CROPS.
NOTE: The data set WORK.SCORE1 has 36 observations and 13 variables.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE LOGISTIC printed page 1237.

15027      proc logistic data=Crops outmodel=work.CropModel;
15028      model Crop=x1-x4 / link=glogit;
15029      score data=Crops out=Score2;
15030      store CropModel2;
15031      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is fitting the generalized logit model. The logits modeled contrast each response level against the reference level (Crop='Sugarbeets'). 
      Use the response variable option REF= if you want to change the reference level.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: The LOGISTIC procedure generated the model item store WORK.CROPMODEL2.
